Fix partitions ${\lambda}/{\mu}$ and ${
u}$. Let $\psi_k:GT_{k{\lambda}/k{\mu},k{
u}}	o GT_{{\lambda}/{\mu},{
u}}$ be the map sending a pattern to the unique lexicographically largest pattern $G'$ satisfying $kG'\leq_{\operatorname*{lex}}G$. For a fixed $G\in GT_{{\lambda}/{\mu},{
u}}$, consider the fibre $\psi_k^{-1}(G)$. **Fibre polynomiality conjecture.** For any fixed $G\in GT_{{\lambda}/{\mu},{
u}}$, the size of the inverse image of $G$ under $\psi_k^{-1}$ is a polynomial in $k$. This is a later formulation involving fibres of the map $\psi_k$; the source does not provide a proof or resolution.
